The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says the ticket is one known bug with one fix queued. The
reports say otherwise. #4471 holds three problems, and only one of them has the queued fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix does not touch the booking-v3 form hint or the one-day
moves. Those reports stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

The desk's own cause table, over the export as it came. The one-day moves are its footnote:
they are counted under the parser, where the desk files them by tenant.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each problem has its own ticket in
[mike131/mega-what-it-shows](https://github.com/mike131/mega-what-it-shows/issues):

1. **The parser** ([#1](https://github.com/mike131/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1)): the shared
   parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant books 7 April, and the invite says
   4 July. The fix that #4471 queued is for this problem.
2. **The booking-v3 hint** ([#2](https://github.com/mike131/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2)): the
   booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it tells them, and
   the form reads their date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not reach it. Only
   reports sent through that form belong here.
3. **The one-day moves** ([#3](https://github.com/mike131/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3)): the
   date moves by one day in the same month, and two people in different time zones get
   different days for one meeting. No month and day are swapped. The desk listed these reports
   in `desk-notes.json`. The cause table counts them under the parser, by tenant.

## How the reports got merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on subject alone, and
nobody reads the body. The same subject lines cover all three problems, so the rule put them in
one ticket. The cause comes from the tenant's locale, its booking form and the channel
(`causes.ts`), and from what the body says. Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser:
do not count by it.

## For the desk

- Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. Check the hint and one-day tickets first.
- When the reporter's tenant runs booking-v3 and they came in through the form, file the report
  under the hint ticket.
- When the body names the same month and a day one off, file it under the one-day ticket and
  add its id to `desk-notes.json`.

